{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Goal\nCut rebar 0.15.0 from current `main`, following docs/releasing.md (steps 1, 1a, 2, then verify 3-5). 0.14.0 (2026-10-30) is the latest on PyPI, GitHub Releases and the MCP Registry, and `main` carries 143 commits since v0.14.0.\n\nWhy a minor (0.15.0), not a patch: `[Unreleased]` in CHANGELOG.md holds 2 entries marked BREAKING (pre-1.0) — the retired warn-class config/env tombstones (e21f3240cd0) and the removed canary `github-api` heartbeat source (73e90b296e2). docs/api-stability.md puts pre-1.0 breaking changes in a minor release, and no earlier patch release carried a BREAKING entry.\n\n## Preconditions (checked 2026-11-09)\n- `release.yml` publishes PyPI and the MCP Registry through OIDC; no stored secret is needed. The `pypi` environment requires reviewer JoeOakhartNava and allows only the `main` branch; `gh` is authenticated as JoeOakhartNava.\n- Version is carried by pyproject.toml `[project].version`, server.json top-level `version` and every `packages[].version`, uv.lock (root package entry) and tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json (`__version__`).\n- Homebrew tap `navapbc/homebrew-rebar`: `Formula/rebar.rb` is at 0.13.1, and `autobump.yml` is in state `disabled_inactivity` (last run 2026-10-28). It cannot be dispatched until a maintainer re-enables it; re-enabling is a repository setting outside this ticket's authority, so it is escalated to the operator rather than done here.\n\n## Plan\n1. Bump 0.14.0 -> 0.15.0 in lockstep: pyproject.toml `version`; server.json top-level `version` and every `packages[].version`.\n2. `uv lock`, then `make install` (so the editable install reports 0.15.0), then `python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --update`. Check `git diff` shows only version changes in uv.lock and only the `__version__` value in tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json.\n3. CHANGELOG.md: `[Unreleased]` is already curated, so retitle it `## [0.15.0] - 2026-11-09` (no `make changelog`), open a fresh empty `## [Unreleased]` above it, and add a `[0.15.0]: .../compare/v0.14.0...v0.15.0` footer link. Hand-curate: add user-facing fixes merged since v0.14.0 that the section does not yet cover, keep both entries marked BREAKING, no ticket noise, no financial figures.\n4. One commit with a `rebar-ticket:` trailer for this ticket and a DCO sign-off (`git commit -s`).\n5. Local checks: `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` (no timeout) and `python -m build && python -m twine check dist/*`.\n6. `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main%hashtag=rebar-session-a85e3cd3-9e61-4f25-9de4-cd740e853b4d` (not WIP). At LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 and 0 unresolved comments, land with `scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py <n> --revision <full sha>`; wait for the GitHub mirror's `main` to contain the merged commit.\n7. `gh workflow run release.yml --ref main -f version=0.15.0`; watch the run; when it pauses at the `pypi` environment, approve via the runbook's `pending_deployments` REST call with the JSON body sent through `--input`.\n8. Verify channels: PyPI JSON API, `gh release view v0.15.0`, the `mcp_registry` job result plus the registry search API, and Homebrew. Post-publish probe: `pipx install \"nava-rebar[mcp]==0.15.0\" --force`, then `REBAR=<pipx bin>/rebar python scripts/probe_rebar.py` (no `PROBE_LIVE`).\n\nFailure handling: a release-run failure before publish is debugged and, if it needs a code fix, fixed through Gerrit and re-dispatched. After PyPI publishes, nothing is re-uploaded (PyPI is immutable): a failed later job (github_release, mcp_registry) is re-run with `gh run rerun <run> --failed`, both jobs being idempotent; a defective published artifact is reported for yank + new patch version.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] pyproject.toml, server.json (top-level and every packages[].version), uv.lock and tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json all carry 0.15.0, and CHANGELOG.md has a `## [0.15.0] - 2026-11-09` section that keeps both BREAKING entries, an empty `## [Unreleased]` above it, and a `[0.15.0]` compare link; the commit carries the rebar-ticket trailer and DCO sign-off.\n- [ ] `make verify` and `twine check` pass locally on the release commit.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The release commit lands on `main` through Gerrit at LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1; evidence: Gerrit change number and merged SHA, which the GitHub mirror's `main` contains.\n      provenance: environment=production Gerrit rebar.solutions.navateam.com + GitHub mirror navapbc/rebar; principal=RebarBotNava (Gerrit REST) and JoeOakhartNava (gh); privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — read from the change's DETAILED_LABELS and git ls-remote of origin main after submit\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The `release.yml` run dispatched from `main` with version=0.15.0 completes with conclusion success; evidence: run id and per-job conclusions.\n      provenance: environment=GitHub Actions navapbc/rebar; principal=JoeOakhartNava (gh); privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — read via gh run view on the dispatched run\n- [ ] [non-codebase] PyPI serves nava-rebar 0.15.0; evidence: `info.version` from https://pypi.org/pypi/nava-rebar/json.\n      provenance: environment=production pypi.org; principal=anonymous public JSON API; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — read via curl of the public JSON API after publish\n- [ ] [non-codebase] GitHub Release v0.15.0 exists, is marked Latest, and has the sdist and wheel attached, with tag v0.15.0 at the released SHA; evidence: `gh release view v0.15.0`.\n      provenance: environment=github.com navapbc/rebar Releases; principal=JoeOakhartNava (gh); privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — read via gh release view and gh api releases/latest\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The MCP Registry lists io.github.navapbc/rebar 0.15.0 as latest; evidence: the `mcp_registry` job conclusion and the registry search API response.\n      provenance: environment=production registry.modelcontextprotocol.io; principal=anonymous public search API; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — read via curl of the v0/servers search endpoint after the run\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Homebrew `Formula/rebar.rb` in navapbc/homebrew-rebar points at the 0.15.0 sdist, or, while autobump.yml stays disabled, the blocker is escalated to the operator and filed as a linked bug; evidence: the formula's url line or the bug id.\n      provenance: environment=github.com navapbc/homebrew-rebar; principal=JoeOakhartNava (gh); privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — read via gh api contents of Formula/rebar.rb and the workflow state\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The post-publish probe against the pipx-installed 0.15.0 binary reports 0 failed; evidence: the `PROBE RESULT` line.\n      provenance: environment=local macOS host, pipx venv installed from production PyPI; principal=local operator user; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — scripts/probe_rebar.py run against the pipx-installed binary\n\n## File impact (expected)\n- pyproject.toml\n- server.json\n- uv.lock\n- tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json\n- CHANGELOG.md"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794256294871992001,"uuid":"ab92dff1-4c10-4730-9d12-d4f8647c1978"}